WEBVTT

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:09.980
Airi, it's cramped.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.290
You're too big, that's all!

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.140
No, you're small.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.740
You're getting on my nerves...

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.870
I'll make chawanmushi when we get back.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.480
Hmph! If we get back in one piece.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.060
Hibiki's in danger!

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.440
C'mon, go faster!

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.670
Who are you to Mr. Hibiki?

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.670
We're his friends!

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.920
Please, go faster.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.130
I'm goin' as fast as I can.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.150
It's almost time.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.030
The Septentrion will
attack here, won't they?

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.030
That's right.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:27.810
The third of them will appear
here, per the long-standing

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.250
covenant of the Hotsuin family.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.710
There's so much about the enemy
that even we at JP's don't know.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.910
Do you honestly think you can
fight them on your own?

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.990
What do you think, Ronaldo?

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:45.750
Our demons are much stronger
than the ones JP's uses.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.810
Going forward, WE shall
protect the people.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.730
There you have it.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.900
But who the heck made this app?

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.070
You don't think it's dangerous to use
something of unknown origin?

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:03.490
It simply means we're not the only
ones opposed to JP's methods.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.770
Nicaea...

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.580
Everything started with this app.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.860
I have the ability to summon demons
more powerful than anyone else's.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:26.590
But if a power's use is unknown,
it's no better than being powerless.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:37.760
You're Hibiki Kuze, scouted by the
Tokyo bureau chief, aren't you?

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:38.990
Yes.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.150
Why are you with the resistance?

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:46.400
I thought I wouldn't be able
to save everyone at JP's.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.410
So JP's is no good?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.580
The bureau chief has a rough
way of doing things, but...

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.600
But it must be obeyed.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.840
Is that what JP's is about?

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.760
Yes, that's right.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.900
Yamato Hotsuin...

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.800
Many people have died by his orders.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.720
Were those deaths necessary?

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:12.600
Can you chalk it up as unavoidable?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.810
In the end, doing that led to the
least amount of deaths.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.360
That's the bureau chief's thinking.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.690
I can understand that thinking.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.200
But...

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.680
But...!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.790
Your heart can't accept it, can it?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:38.040
Did you have the choice not to fight?

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.990
If I didn't know I had this
power, I wouldn't fight.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.210
I was a normal high-school
student before.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.410
But you fight now that you have power.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.180
How brave.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.560
No, that's not it.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.560
If Yamato Hotsuin were in
the right, I'd help him.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.570
But I can't obey him without
knowing if he's right for sure.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.570
So Ronaldo Kuriki IS right?

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.950
At the very least, he's not someone
who would sacrifice others.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.580
Hibiki!

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.330
Someone here says he's your friend,
but is he really--?

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.370
Hibiki!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:18.670
Daichi!

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.190
You idiot!

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.520
What are you doin' on your own?!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.490
I'm sorry, Daichi.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.810
We were worried.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:28.930
Sorry.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.350
Your friends?

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:31.680
Yes.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.640
I'm so glad we made it in time!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:35.720
Huh?

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.550
Those guys are JP's, right?

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.640
Shouldn't we keep an eye on them?

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.860
They're Hibiki's friends, aren't they?

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.190
It'll be fine, right?

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.070
I'm gonna go buy some coffee.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:47.660
'Kay.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.620
A dead face clip of me?

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.250
It came to our cell phones.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:57.870
After we'd already sneaked aboard the train,
so we were freaked out.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.990
Sneaked? Without JP's permission?

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.460
That's got nothin' to do with it.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.880
YOU'RE more important, right?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.930
How is the Nagoya branch?

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:16.350
Communications remain
suspended on their end.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.350
The infiltration unit remains missing.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:23.560
Daichi Shijima and Io Nitta,
who disappeared from the Osaka Main Bureau,

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.050
remain out of contact.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.440
Couldn't they have fled?

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.780
They may well have.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.860
There's no need to bring
this to anyone else.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.250
I'll deal with it personally.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:33.660
Ma'am.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.200
I hope they're both all right...

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.840
Okay Hibiki, let's hurry and go back.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.370
Uh, to Tokyo!

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:44.500
Daichi...

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.290
Hm?

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.550
I can't go back.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.300
Huh?!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.470
Why not?
Huh?!

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.180
A Septentrion will appear here soon.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:56.400
Knowing that, there's
no way I can just leave.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.780
This isn't the time to talk like that!

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.940
Those dead face clips aren't wrong.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.520
You know that, right?

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.270
Prior knowledge will
let you escape that.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:06.480
We couldn't in Osaka--! Uh...

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:15.330
Jeez! I'LL protect you!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.230
We can beat that dead face clip, huh?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.760
Me, too.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.800
I'll protect you too, Hibiki.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.130
So... Don't go running off.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.340
Taking it on singlehandedly is not good.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.670
I know that.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.140
But...

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.910
Couldn't help them?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.350
Looks to me like you've
been dragged into this.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:44.210
Great power drags people in.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.940
Being with me is more
dangerous than anything.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.670
What are you saying? Dammit!

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.920
Power has nothing to do with it!

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:58.830
I can't abandon my childhood friend
when he's at his wits' end, can I?!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.020
Daichi...

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:07.190
I-It's better than bein'
on your own, right?

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:09.960
Things are sure to go
better if we join forces.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.970
Thank you.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.710
They tell us to hurry
and clear things up,

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.180
but there's no end to this!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.100
'Cause Ronaldo and them
went on the rampage.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:29.900
Wh-What the?

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:33.610
That was close.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.530
I swear! It's because
you're too big, Jungo!

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.450
Who're you two?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.410
We're surrounded.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.160
D-Do as we planned!

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.580
Understood.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:44.620
Damn you insurgents!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.010
We've come to take this base back!

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.380
JP's Summoners?!

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.210
Where is your leader?

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.130
Why would I let you meet him?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.220
Violence is not good.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.700
Demonic summoning, huh? Suits me fine!

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.200
Airi, you look happy.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.060
Cait Sith!

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.900
Neko Shogun.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.370
Let's go!

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.920
These guys are tough!

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:30.740
What's the matter?

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.740
I ain't had enough fun yet!

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:33.760
"Fun"?

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.550
No, it's not fun!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:41.170
JP's Summoners.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.930
Would you mind stopping there, please?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.760
Your demons are quite strong.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:51.070
Well. This has gotten crazy, huh?

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.230
You're the resistance leader?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.150
Nah, no way. That's him.

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:59.440
You cannot beat these two. Fall back.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.580
Sir!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.450
You? You attacked this place yesterday?

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.290
I'm Ronaldo Kuriki.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.380
Though you appear to
be JP's team members,

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:12.380
you speak as if scouted without
having been told the reason.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.460
"Reason"?

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:14.360
Yes.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.340
Why do you follow JP's without question?

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.180
Think about it. What is proper?

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.680
Shut up with your talk! I'm for justice!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.890
Hey, ain't this kinda bad?

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.150
Put it on the main monitor.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.620
Airi. I thought we came to talk.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.040
He'll listen to us after I've won!

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.290
Please stop this!

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.130
This isn't the time for
human to fight human, is it?

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:53.750
Hibiki...

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:54.920
He's right.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.380
Who're you?! You're talkin' crap!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.840
We can talk once you've surrendered!

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:05.190
Hey! This is...!

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:10.730
Airi.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.190
What's this shaking?

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:13.670
Ronaldo!

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.810
Manifestation readings
have suddenly increased!

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.740
A Septentrion will appear!

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.570
Playtime is over.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.660
Looks like it, Airi.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.490
I'm telling you, this isn't a game!

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.700
Hurry and pinpoint its
manifest location.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.750
Wait! This is...

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:31.740
Where?

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.790
The manifest location is...

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.510
It's HERE!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.300
What did you say?

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.470
Uh, what? What?!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:43.510
Hibiki!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.960
Command center to all hands!

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:23.970
Everyone other than members I've chosen,
head for the shelters at once!

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.930
You all will be helping me, too.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.140
Huh? Who put you in charge?

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.930
Airi. The enemy is over THERE.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.270
You guys, too!

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.490
Attack from all sides!

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.700
You don't gotta tell me!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.410
It's tough!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.740
This is bad, ain't it?

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.450
So long as there's no damage aboveground,
it's actually a good thing.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:52.710
We'll defeat it here!

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:56.790
How's that?!

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:57.540
Did it work?

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.090
It didn't work.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.130
Then I'll do it till it DOES work!

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.220
It's not taking any
damage from our attacks?

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.400
Wh-What?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.030
Not good.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:26.670
Hey, what are you doing?

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:27.700
It's coming!

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:39.670
A blackout?

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.200
Huh? What did it do?

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.130
Ronaldo! The power line's down!

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:47.180
We're switchin' over
to backup power now.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:50.370
It wanted to disrupt
the base's functions!

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:57.310
I see. It's shown up at
an interesting point.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:02.440
Still, I think it's a
bit cruel to the humans.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.880
If we lose systems here...

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.660
we'll be unable to sustain
the Ryumyaku battier.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.740
What's gonna happen?!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.660
Nagoya will be destroyed.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.290
Destroyed?

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.450
If we take another hit,
Nagoya is done for.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.290
This is bad, ain't it?

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:25.340
H-Hey! If our attacks don't work,
then what do we do?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.680
I can't allow any more of this.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.440
Suzaku! Burn it!

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:44.900
I won't let anyone be killed!

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.740
A-Awesome.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.320
Who's that?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.660
Kuze Hibiki.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.120
He's our hope.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:05.590
Hibiki!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:07.340
Daichi!

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:10.340
I told you, didn't I? You're not alone.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:15.940
For such a sad-lookin' sack,
he sure brought a powerful demon.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:17.020
Nice!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.350
Sarasvati!

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:32.180
Sarasvati's has an acquired Drain skill.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.870
It will weaken the enemy.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.290
Awesome!

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:46.420
It split!

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.670
Hey, what does that think it's doing?

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.420
Oh, no! Suzaku!

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:07.940
Kikuri-Hime!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:20.430
Not good. That beam was
on the dead face clip!

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:23.250
Hibiki, run!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.020
Dammit. Byakko!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:35.550
Hang on!

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:56.570
Hibiki!

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.740
No!

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.770
Don't make me do that again.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:32.880
Yamato Hotsuin!

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:34.360
Why...?

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:36.820
Cerberus.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.220
This is...

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.780
A human is overwriting
a demon's abilities?!

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.140
It can't be!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.480
This is what the Hotsuin family's
blood has wrought?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.940
No. It's MY power.

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.420
Sir, did you make it?

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.300
Prof. Kanno! How are you transmitting?

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.090
I took it back.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.170
What was that?!

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:38.090
You guys had your hands full.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:42.370
You were timing for this all along!

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.790
It's the same method you guys use.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.880
He should be in Tokyo, right?

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:51.060
How'd he get here?

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.980
The transport Terminal was still under repair,
not yet operational.

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:55.530
Yes.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:59.110
The bureau chief himself supplied
the remaining magical powers.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.780
That's not something a human can do.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:04.700
That monster!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.210
Communications with the
Nagoya Brach have been restored!

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.460
The infiltration team survived.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:10.880
The base has been recaptured!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:15.750
Sir! You would've died if you'd failed.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.720
Why do something so dangerous?!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.640
You...

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:28.650
If you have that kind of power,
you should've been able to fight all alone!

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:30.440
So why?

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:33.310
Why did everyone die by your orders?!

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.250
How foolish.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:38.400
It's necessary in order
to face Judgment Day.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.610
WHY is it necessary?

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:44.450
I don't know what you're thinking!

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:48.310
After tomorrow, defeating
the Septentrion

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:50.910
will require pawns to act on my accord.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.540
"Pawns"?

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.710
Hibiki Kuze.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.630
You have become an exceptional pawn.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:02.510
How dare you call people "pawns"?!

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:04.970
Emotions are meaningless to pawns.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.800
You will return to my side
and follow my orders.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:13.440
Can that save people?
Can it save the world?!

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:14.900
Yes.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:16.310
Hibiki!

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:18.780
Pay no attention to what that man says!

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.280
The former detective, eh?

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:23.240
Yamato Hotsuin.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:28.370
I cannot allow a world,
a future where the weak are simply expunged!

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:32.160
The egalitarianism of which
you speak is a pipe dream.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:35.920
If you can lick one another's
wounds and survive, do so.

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.840
But the invaders will grant no mercy.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.130
No one will survive that.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.300
So if YOU survive past Judgment Day,
just what do you intend?

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:51.390
I already know that with the world in chaos,
you plan to become its ruler!

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:54.310
Rule?

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:58.480
So civilians get dicked around, huh?

00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:02.320
He who is blessed with strength
should become the guide.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.530
That is all.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.570
Everyone who supports JP's,

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:10.330
this is what the Hotsuin Family
has prepared for since antiquity!

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:12.830
Curse your blood-stained family!

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.580
You would challenge me?

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:22.950
You pissant.

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:24.550
I won't be easy on you.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.540
What do you think you're doing?

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:38.690
Please stop.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:39.650
Why?

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:44.030
If you're saying you're going to hurt people,
then I will stop you.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.530
I don't understand the person you are!

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:49.870
It's not necessary that you understand.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.540
Things have gotten rather
sad, haven't they?

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:00.790
Hey.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:06.970
I never thought fellow Sparkling Ones
would duke it out.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:08.720
Bastard.

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:12.390
This is the first time
all three of us have met.

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:13.880
You're...

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:15.430
Alcor.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:17.490
Hibiki.

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:23.150
Yamato came here because
he saw your dead face clip.

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:24.490
Huh?

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:27.320
Blabbermouth.
